{
  "abstract": "We organize MTT calculations by explicit closure standard and source provenance. Embedded renormalized-Standard-Model equivalence is closed at the adopted one-shared-physical-primitive/measured-profile standard: the final audit passes 12/12 obligations using selected multi-loop transport, the 27-by-27 operator architecture, charged-flavor and CKM rows, Higgs/threshold support, and imported standard SM quantization. Independent structural results now include the native faithful Standard Model gauge group, an anomaly-free 48-state chiral carrier, a completed 96-dimensional finite triple at profile tier, an exact one-Higgs projector, and a zero-parameter 10/10 finite gauge/ghost spectrum source. These achievements do not yet derive the measured gauge and Yukawa values: the strict program remains 2/9, with U2 and U4 closed. The roadmap therefore records named source objects, scope guards, dependencies, and reproducible acceptance tests for every stronger claim.",
